.TH SDL_PRINTF_FORMAT_STRING 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_PRINTF_FORMAT_STRING \- Macro that annotates function params as printf-style format strings.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_PRINTF_FORMAT_STRING _Printf_format_string_
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If we were to annotate
.BR fprintf :

.IP
.EX
int fprintf(FILE *f, SDL_PRINTF_FORMAT_STRING const char *fmt, ...);
.EE
.PP

This notes that
.BR fmt
should be a printf-style format string\[char46] The compiler or other analysis tools can warn when this doesn\(aqt appear to be the case\[char46]
.PP
On compilers without this annotation mechanism, this is defined to nothing\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

